+ *
+ * `summaryInputBudgetTokens` is a fold-in plan, not a capacity measure: it
+ * discounts the window by 20% and reserves the whole output, so a chain that
+ * physically fits the window can fail it. Judging the live chain with that
+ * budget would silently return to the cut-prefix shape on requests the provider
+ * would have accepted. Capacity is therefore measured on the request itself --
+ * system, tools, messages and the output allowance -- which is exactly what the
+ * provider will count.
