+/**
+ * Locate the retained tail inside a live chain by content and prove that the
+ * excerpt naming it is unique there.
+ *
+ * A message count cannot name the boundary: provider serialization merges and
+ * expands messages (a trailing `Continue.` pad, a turn-scoped developer control
+ * split in two, tool results folded into one user turn), so "the first N
+ * messages" is not the same position on the wire. Content is. The excerpt is
+ * trimmed to the shortest prefix that still selects exactly one message; when
+ * no prefix of it does, the caller must refuse rather than guess -- a model
+ * obeying an ambiguous excerpt stops at the first match, which can sit before
+ * the real boundary, and those messages are then in neither the summary nor the
+ * replayed tail.
